### What is the N-Queens problem?

Place n queens on an n-by-n chessboard so that no two queens attack each other. Queens attack along rows, columns, and diagonals. Since we place exactly one queen per row, the row conflict is automatically avoided. The challenge is avoiding column and diagonal conflicts.

This is LeetCode 51 (N-Queens) and 52 (N-Queens II for count only).

